          "name": "Nika Becker",
          "search_text": "ina becker charactering the metabolites released by coral-associated endozoicomonas symbiosis with microorganisms is vital for reef-building corals. in addition to symbiodiniaceae, bacteria are thought to provide many essential nutrients to their hosts. genomic and transcriptomic data have been used to propose multiple functional roles of the bacterial genus endozoicomonas, one of the most widespread coral associates. some of these functions include the synthesis and provision of metabolites such as b-vitamins, hormones, and antimicrobial substances. here, we characterised the metabolites exuded by a coral-associated endozoicomonas in pure culture under different conditions (temperature, salinity, ph) using liquid chromatography coupled with mass spectrometry. these data will provide a baseline of its biosynthetic potential and identify target metabolites that will be knocked out in future experiments in hospite to assess their function in the holobiont.",
