      "distance_km": 13597.9,
      "search_text": "duke university ty roach ty roach engineering climate-wise reefs at scale: phage-based precision medicine, ai-enabled assisted evolution, and whole-ecosystem restoration we are advancing a suite of complementary approaches that apply ecological precision medicine and ai-enabled assisted evolution coupled with scalable deployment platforms to restore entire reef ecosystems in a climate-wise manner. specifically, we have developed single-polyp multi-omics methods that allow for holobiont-informed interventions, including phage therapies that harness historically overlooked viral regulation of coral resilience, as well as precision probiotics, and mucus/microbiome transplants to enhance coral stress tolerance and disease resistance. in parallel, we integrate resilience-linked biomarkers with ai-enabled assisted evolution to forecast and amplify thermal tolerance. using novel ai architectures, we have identified metabolomic biomarkers that predict coral bleaching susceptibility with up to 100% accuracy, enabling high-confidence selection of individuals for selective breeding. corals produced through this pipeline exhibit >20% increases in heat tolerance in a single generation, representing an unprecedented leap for how adaptive capacity can be built into restoration. because coral-only restoration efforts often fail, we have embedded these techniques and others within a whole-ecosystem restoration approach using coral reef arks, modular midwater reef structures designed to rebuild entire coral reefs along with their associated biodiversity, trophic interactions, and ecosystem services. in early deployments, arks have proven more than twice as effective as conventional restoration measures. this whole-ecosystem approach provides a pathway from laboratory innovation to field-scale, climate-ready reef restoration. together, this integrated framework links holobiont-centered precision medicine techniques, ai-guided selective breeding, and whole-ecosystem restoration into a scalable roadmap for future-proofing reefs under accelerating environmental change.",
