          "name": "Kate Brown",
          "search_text": "kate brown island leadership inspiring impact for the last 20 years a group of island leaders across the island regions of the world have both catalysed and been inspired by a set of initiatives which have had a significant impact on island and ocean biodiversity. starting with the announcement of the micronesia challenge in 2006 (at the same time parties to the convention on biodiversity adopted the programme of work on island biodiversity),  the coral triangle initiative, caribbean challenge initiative, the best challenge - in europe overseas, the seychelles debt swap, niue's large scale mpa and the aloha+challenge this set of leaders has faced the implementation challenge - how you move from science and policy to on ground implementation. these large political commitments are really a story as well about how we move to scale implementation and a great willingness between these islands to share lessons learned and create a global platform for island advocacy. they have also led the development or strengthening of national and regional trust funds (caribbean biodiversity fund and national trust funds in the caribbean region, niue oceanwide trust, cti ctf, micronesia conservation trust, seychelles conservation and climate adaptation trust fund) which have been a game changer for these islands in terms of building stronger capacity for financing conservation through locally led mechanisms that last beyond project cycles. this presentation will speak to what has been learnt throughout 20 years of significant island leadership and how islands can continue to play this leadership role in catalysing action for what comes next.",
