          "name": "Nikol Slynkova",
          "search_text": "nikol slynkova distribution and characteristics of microplastics in a coral reef environment: heron island, great barrier reef, australia coral reefs are among the most biodiverse ecosystems on earth with great barrier reef (gbr) being the world's largest coral reef systems.  despite its ecological importance, there is limited understanding of the abundance and distribution of microplastics (mps) in the gbr. for the first time, this study aims to quantify and characterize mps (>25 µm) in water and in sediment from six sites around the heron island. a total of 48 surface water, 27 inter-tidal sediment (is), and 18 sub-tidal sediment (ss) samples were collected. water samples were collected using a custom-built high-volume sampling device, while sediment samples were collected using transect (is) and grab sampling (ss) approach. a comprehensive quality assurance and quality control (qa/qc) protocol was implemented during sampling, processing and analysis, to ensure data reliability. a total of 447 synthetic particles were extracted, with an average abundance of 0.32 ± 0.16 mps/l (water),  21.85 ± 9.55 mps/kg (is),  and 73.89 ± 28.43 mps/kg (ss). particles were predominantly fibers (74% water, 75% is, and 38% ss), and fragments (26% water, 25% is, 62% ss). the polymer composition of mps was analyzed using fourier transform infrared spectroscopy (ftir), revealing polyethylene terephthalate (pet) as the most common polymer type. particles colors were mainly black, pink, and transparent across all three sampling matrices. nevertheless, over 40% of mps extracted were within the size range of 25 – 300 µm, indicating the importance of detecting smaller-sized mps to provide accurate data.",
          "talk_titles": [
            {
              "title": "Distribution and Characteristics of Microplastics in a Coral Reef Environment: Heron Island, Great Barrier Reef, Australia",
              "primary": true,
              "talk_id": "b30d9d3d-bce9-46e2-bc55-e05999e40502"
            }
          ],
