      "search_text": "michigan state university sarah vandiepenbos sarah vandiepenbos enzyme-mediated lysolipid dynamics are associated with coral bleaching resistance the coral–algal symbiosis is foundational to reef ecosystems and threatened by bleaching, where heat stress causes the loss of algal symbionts. bleaching susceptibility varies by symbiont lineage: durusdinium-hosting coral are generally more thermotolerant than cladocopium. a betaine lipid synthesized only by algal symbionts, 1,2-diacylglyceryl-3-(o-carboxyhydroxymethylcholine) (dgcc), is highly abundant in the membranes of dinoflagellates, with a 16:0 fatty acid moiety on the sn-1 position and a 22:6 fatty acid moiety on the sn-2 position. using a model population of montipora capitata, we demonstrated that durusdinium are associated with higher levels of lysolipids. lysolipids form via enzyme-mediated hydrolysis, with lyso-dgcc forming after a fatty acid moiety is cleaved from dgcc. in a novel lysolipid accumulation timecourse experiment, galaxea fascicularis tentacles hosting either durusdinium or cladocopium symbionts were incubated for 24 hours in artificial seawater at room temperature, then lipid extracts were analyzed by lc-ms/ms. we found higher abundance of lyso-dgcc (16:0) in durusdinium-hosting corals compared to cladocopium due to cleavage at the sn-2 position, releasing the 22:6 polyunsaturated fatty acid. we also detected an abundance of lyso-dgcc(22:6), indicating that the sn-1 position is cleaved as well but in lesser proportion. durusdinium-hosting corals synthesized more lysolipids than cladocopium, indicating a higher phospholipase activity that may correlate with bleaching tolerance. another mechanistic possibility is that an acyltransferase adds fatty acids to a dgcc head group, since dgcc (22:6/22:6) molecules are also abundant. to examine whether corals regulate the expression of phospholipases and acyltransferases under temperature stress, we compared gene expression in cladocopium- and durusdinium-hosting montipora capitata, illustrating dynamic enzymatic regulation of lysolipids and their role in bleaching susceptibility and climate resilience.",
