          "name": "Sarah O'Connor",
          "search_text": "sarah o'connor coral data access evolution - adapting large-scale program data management to meet community needs the fair guiding principles, published in 2016, significantly boosted data sharing (findability and accessibility) in the scientific community, yet achieving true interoperability and reusability remains a persistent challenge.the national oceanic and atmospheric administration's coral reef conservation program (crcp) mirrored this open data movement, shifting from offline to online data access. however, despite making data accessible, crcp found that stakeholder needs were not met because the program was not producing the desired data products. a major hurdle to interoperability within crcp is integrating data from multiple sources to gain a cohesive regional perspective on reef health. even when using the same methodology, data collected by different offices often varies in formatting, such as column names, units of measurement, or granularity. these inconsistencies complicate national-scale data integration, analysis, and reporting. historically, this has led to reports taking years to produce due to the extensive time required for data translation, and the lack of data consistency has hindered the development of data visualization tools. we will detail the evolution of crcp's data management, including the shift from offline to online data distribution, and share key lessons learned. increased data sharing initially exposed quality control concerns, prompting workflow improvements and additional data access points. discussions with stakeholders captured further issues and identified the need for aggregated data summaries to answer managers’ questions. recognizing this demand led to a redesign of the crcp website and the development of the national coral reef monitoring program data visualization tool. this tool allows users to graph and download summarized fish, benthic, sea water chemistry, and socioeconomic data variables across various geographic scales. the effort to make the underlying raw data for the ncrmp tool accessible has driven significant quality improvements across the entire data life cycle and established a solid foundation for data management across all funded projects.",
