          "name": "George Huster",
          "search_text": "george huster proteomics reveals significant differences in selectively bred corals when under heat stress as part of our coral selective breeding project, two sub-populations of acropora digitifera, one bred from high heat tolerance parents and the other from low tolerance parents, were exposed to a natural mild heat stress event. despite visual bleaching being similar, the proteomes are significantly different, revealing a tiered heat stress response.",
