          "name": "Tracy Ainsworth",
          "search_text": "tracy ainsworth changing coral health in the south pacific: a norfolk island perspective coral disease is an escalating global threat to reef ecosystems, driving rapid declines in foundational coral taxa and undermining ecosystem resilience. even remote, seemingly pristine regions are not insulated from these impacts. at the subtropical reefs of norfolk island, multiple disease states are occurring on the inshore coral reef–including tissue-loss syndromes and growth anomalies– and these disease are occurring simultaneously in multiple key reef-building corals. this multi-species outbreak has been associated with rapid colony mortality, disrupted tissue structure, altered microbial interactions, and evidence of reduced reproductive capacity, indicating limited potential for natural recovery. together, these patterns highlight the vulnerability of isolated reef systems and emphasise the need to better understand and manage the cumulative impacts from land-based sources that drive coral disease dynamics under increasing environmental stress.",
