        {
          "name": "Róisín Hayden",
          "search_text": "róisín hayden priorities and challenges for assessing post-bleaching recovery on coral reefs as anthropogenic stress continues to ravage coral reefs, researchers and managers alike are playing a desperate game of catch-up. given the limited chance of halting climate change, priorities now shift towards enhancing reef resistance and recovery in the dwindling intervals between bleaching events. yet, while abundant literature exists on the processes up to and during bleaching, little is understood about the aftermath. symbiont populations may be rapidly re-established, for example, but other important health indicators like growth and fecundity may take years to be fully restored, with exact timelines remaining unclear. in the last decade, the number of studies addressing coral recovery has started to increase, but still only represent a fraction of those focused on bleaching. fundamental questions, from species-specific recovery potential to when exactly a coral is considered “recovered”, remain unanswered. \r\nin this study, we present an overview of the existing literature on coral recovery, aiming to (1) summarise the current knowledge of how critical functions are restored post-bleaching, from a cellular to ecosystem level; (2) examine important research gaps that may improve management and risk prediction efforts; and (3) highlight the challenges of designing and executing recovery experiments. we further explore how recovery potential may be altered by recurrent heat stress, presenting a case study of pocillopora damicornis exposed to different seasonal temperature regimes. finally, we propose the development of a multi-species framework to predict recovery potential across different levels of bleaching severity. the fate of coral reefs is not solely determined by which species will bleach, or not. rather, it’s those species that will recover, and recover quickly, that can hold the line against future climate change.",
          "talk_titles": [
            {
              "title": "Priorities and Challenges for Assessing Post-Bleaching Recovery on Coral Reefs",
              "primary": true,
              "talk_id": "a3d77ba4-d492-4a8e-99d5-a56655491b30"
            }
          ],
          "person_key": "icrs-p-00736",
          "attended": true
        }
